Third-party rules shipped inside Canyon
---------------------------------------

gate/opengrep/sast-rules.tar is GitLab's sast-rules (https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/security-products/sast-rules),
tag v2.10.1, commit 53bf5cf6df3c51b6c02110f5a638b5e6213666cd, unmodified, the rule files of these folders only:

  python, java, javascript, csharp, scala               MIT, Copyright (c) GitLab Inc. (LICENSE in the archive)
  go                                                    Apache License 2.0 (rules derived from gosec; each file's header;
                                                        LICENSE.Apache-2.0 in the archive)
  rules/lgpl/javascript, rules/lgpl/java,
  rules/lgpl/kotlin                                     GNU LGPL v3.0 (rules derived from njsscan, FindSecBugs and
                                                        mobsfscan; rules/lgpl/LICENSE and COPYING.GPL-3.0 in the archive)

Left out: c (GPL-2.0), rules/lgpl-cc (Commons Clause), rules/gitlab (GitLab EE), and rules/lgpl's
oc and swift. Each rule file keeps its upstream licence header. The archive is rebuilt from the pinned commit by
`make vendor-sast-rules`; the source of every file is that commit of the repository above.

